WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:07.327
Some equations have brackets. Let's solve two times the bracket x plus three equals fourteen.

00:07.777 --> 00:14.394
First, multiply the number outside by everything inside. Two times x is two x.

00:14.394 --> 00:16.345
Two times three is six.

00:16.795 --> 00:22.577
Next, take six away from both sides. Fourteen minus six is eight.

00:23.027 --> 00:27.694
Then divide both sides by two. That gives x equals four.

00:28.144 --> 00:34.553
Check it. Four plus three is seven, and two times seven is fourteen. It works.
